From 45415714ff42a3f4959c7b91afa8da2d6c89047e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Himess <semihcvlk53@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 15:27:31 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/8] test(shared): deterministic Profile H tests with a mocked
 provider

19 tests that pin the exact RPC sequence of each verification: H1 caps
reject with no RPC in every mode (and exactly-at-cap passes), the H3
budget formula, H2 code classification and the code-first matrix (empty
code, 7702 rejecting delegate refusing the root key, 7702 empty-success
shim only for a 65-byte root-key signature and off under Profile Q, empty
and reasoned reverts and short returns never falling back, regular code
ERC-1271 only), transport errors not counted, H4 two attempts a block
apart then exhausted, and H8 shadow serving Off while reporting the
would-be rejection with one shared isValidSignature call.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
